    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip accent\">Pattern primer</span><span class=\"chip\">Matrix</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Matrix problems</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">A matrix is an array of rows, and most matrix questions are really about walking it in an unusual order or changing it without a second copy. Learn four moves: shrinking walls for spiral order, i + j and i - j for diagonals, transpose-then-reverse for rotation, and using the matrix itself as scratch memory. Then validate rows, columns and boxes with bitmasks.</p>\r\n"
